From 05f017dce4f6a8f1f1dca8cd7b74494a5b192aaf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:01:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] duck-brain P11: Feetech HD-1910 bus driver (`[bus] driver
 = "feetech"`)

The duck-brain robot has fifteen Feetech HD-1910 servos on a half-duplex
TTL line at 1 Mbit/s, protocol v1, no IMU board on the bus.

- feetech/ (new crate): framing, a streaming parser, deadline reads with
  per-servo results, echo handling, verified register writes, the
  torque-on sequence of the 13-14.10 measurements; an in-memory emulator
  for tests.
- duck-control::feetech::FeetechIo: the tick is one sync_write of 42 and
  one sync_read of 56..62 (56..63 once a second for temperature). A
  servo that does not answer keeps its last position and is counted per
  id. Direction sign per joint, error multiplied by 7.4 / V (smoothed
  lowest servo voltage, clamped 6.0-9.5 V), torque off after 5 ticks
  below 4.5 V, velocity from position difference or register 58. No
  EEPROM writes, no homing_offset, no filters.
- duck-control::host_imu::ImuFeed: where the host-read IMU (P12) hands
  its newest sample to the tick; `robotd --static-imu` feeds a constant
  upright one for bench runs against an emulator.
- RobotIo::adapts_voltage: [policy] voltage_adapt stands down when the
  bus compensates by itself.
- robotd: [feetech] params, startup census, robot.health `feetech`
  block (tick period p50/p99, misses per id, V min/median, temperatures,
  observation age, IMU sample age), degraded on undervoltage cutoff;
  `robotd init` refuses on this bus (robotctl robot init ramps to the
  policy HOME).
- robotctl servo: table / ping / read / write / torque, straight on the
  port with robotd stopped.
